\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Hopkins County came in under 90% of normal in September to October in 35 of 75 years since 1951, and in May to June in 29 years. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, July to August ran 60% of normal and November to December 41%. So far in 2026, January to February sat at 22% and June to July at 160%. Grid 20569 had its driest year in 1963 at 56%, and grid 21171 had its driest in 2010 at 67%.</p>"}
